-serif 9.0pt; text-align:left; color:#000000 )/F 4/M(D:20240920144842-03'00')/NM(d7acb930cdb148c288da8a71ac95f1c3)/Page 1/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:24.3.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2"  style="font-size:6.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal\;font-family:Arial;font-stretch:normal"><p dir="ltr"><span style="font-size:9.0pt;text-align:justify">These entities are located in Dropflight&#8217;s \(the neighboring city to Compelvista\) city graveyard, and created a local urban legend for it due to t\he anomalous characteristics they possess. Normally, they are common statues, with no visible particularities, with religious iconography at most \(saints, angels, nuns, crosses\), however if the date in the calendar shows a day above the number 27, the e\ntities seem to gain sentience. The behavior of the creatures, when active, consists in moving at varied velocities when not observed. The method which they use to move is unknown, and many attempts at capturing said movement ended up with the material co\rrupted or distorted. When a target is set, they adopt an &#8220;entrapment&#8221; strategy, trying to get as close as possible of the target, and looking to block any possible exits, and only that is apparently necessary because, for some still undiscove\red reason, when approaching it, the target starts to show signs of poisoning, which worsens the more time it spends close to the entities, until it eventually succumbs, the poisoning continuing even after death, decomposing the body, until it&#8217;s com\pletely gone. It is speculated that a total of 400 people became victims to these entities, since after their disappearances, in some cases, some organic residue could be found with matches to the victims&#8217;, in places near to the graveyard. It is spe\culated that the reason for this behavior being presented is the relations the place has to the dates of death of the firstborn and the youngest child from the couple formed by Dorgiel Flighter and Marie Lamnert, the former being part of the family tree o\f the city&#8217;s founder, and the latter, the founder of the graveyard and the city&#8217;s public garden. The firstborn died in a 27</span><span style="font-size:10.0pt;text-align:justify;vertical-align:+5.0pt">th</span><span style="font-size:9.0pt;tex\t-align:justify">, and the youngest, on a 35</span><span style="font-size:9.1pt;text-align:justify;vertical-align:+4.5pt">th</span><span style="font-size:9.0pt;text-align:justify">, according to their hospital&#8217;s death certificates.</span></p></body>\)/Rect[45.3301 43.254 571.332 206.874]/Subj(Text Box)/Subtype/FreeText/T( )/Type/Annot>>endobj41 0 obj<</BS<</W 0>>/CA 1/Contents(   Dif)/DA(0 0 0 RG 0 0 0 rg 0 Tc 0 Tw 100 Tz 0 TL 0 Ts 0 Tr /Helv 21.8 Tf)/DS(font: Helvetica,sans-serif 21.8pt; text-align:left; color:#000000 )/F 4/M(D:20240913192048-03'00')/NM(1219d7225def45e683de28447d5ac6ff)/Page 2/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:24.3.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2"  style="font-size:21.8pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:norma\l;font-family:Helvetica,sans-serif;font-stretch:normal"><p dir="ltr"><span style="font-family:Helvetica">   Dif</span></p></body>)/Rect[17.9555 674.711 181.528 700.122]/Subj(Text Box)/Subtype/FreeText/T( )/Type/Annot>>endobj42 0 obj<</BS<</W 0>>/CA 1/Contents(    A)/DA(0 0 0 RG 0 0 0 rg /Helv 21.79505144838562 Tf)/DS(font: Helvetica,sans-serif 21.8pt; text-align:left; color:#000000 )/F 4/M(D:20240913192039-03'00')/NM(45260a535c7d43a6b4ed7b42bf25854f)/Page 2/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:24.3.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2"  style="font-size:21.8pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;fo